From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7530-mmio: unregister DSA when MDIO setup fails

The MMIO frontend registers its DSA switch before creating the child MDIO bus.
If child-bus setup fails, undo the DSA registration before returning the probe
error instead of leaving a partially registered switch behind.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
 gsw/mt7530-mmio.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/gsw/mt7530-mmio.c
+++ b/gsw/mt7530-mmio.c
@@ -66,7 +66,13 @@ mt7988_probe(struct platform_device *pde
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return mt7530_post_register(priv);
+	ret = mt7530_post_register(priv);
+	if (ret) {
+		dsa_unregister_switch(priv->ds);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void mt7988_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
